name: Mastodon work session - audit the account-record contract before a rework
repo: mastodon
contract_symbol: Account
contract_file: app/models/account.rb
# TWO-STEP PROBE SCENARIO (plans/01-author.md), CYCLE 3 - a RE-QUESTION on a live anchor.
# It exists so the next phase can run the mini-bench - both arms, once, at the real wall,
# unscored - against a real baseline. Nothing here is a verdict: no delta is claimed and
# none has been measured on this shape.
#
# Single-prompt session bench (bench/drivers/bench-sense-local.sh): every step is presented
# in ONE prompt and worked in order. Rendered to the agent: the description + each step's
# name and prompt ONLY (checks and gold are NEVER shown). Everything rendered is kept
# NEUTRAL - it states the task, never the answer's shape, file paths, class or method
# names, counts, or which tool to reach for.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SUPERSEDED QUESTION, AND THE NUMBER THAT KILLED IT
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Previous yaml kept at `mastodon.yaml.line-not-file.bak` (cycle 2). Cycle 1's is at
# `mastodon.yaml.class-call-sites.bak`. Cycle 2's axis asked for dependents that "consult
# the record class to settle a question about something else entirely, in whatever form
# the surrounding code already used", and warned that the record's name recurs in those
# files for reasons unrelated to the contract, so the LINE is the discriminator.
#
#   MEASURED (results/loop/mastodon/minibench.md, both arms x1, exit 0, no watchdog,
#   163s and 160s of a 480s wall, both `valid: true`, citation grounding 1.0 both arms):
#     baseline `dependents` 3 of 19 = 0.158   (gate: at or below 0.50)  PASSES
#     sense    `dependents` 3 of 19 = 0.158
#     delta                          = 0.000  (gate: at least +0.50)    FAILS
#
# The question was NOT what failed. The baseline ran ten distinct greps - each guessing a
# different token family, two of them pruning by hand with `grep -vE` - and still came up
# with 3 of 19, with only two `Read` calls in fourteen tool calls. There was no single
# covering grep. The failure was on the INSTRUMENT side: the sense arm never called
# `sense_blast` at all. Its seven MCP calls were `sense_status`, `sense_search`, then five
# `sense_graph` caller walks on `Account::FinderConcern#find_local`, `#find_remote`,
# `#representative`, `#find_local!`, `#find_remote!` - all five flagged `wrong-tool-shape`
# by `tool_use_audit.py`. It anchored on a METHOD SURFACE and never went back up to the
# record class, so the two arms landed on the identical 3 of 19 and the delta was 0.000.
#
# WHAT CHANGED THIS CYCLE (anchor kept, per laws.md ITERATE ON THE QUESTION, KEEP THE ANCHOR):
#   1. STEP 1 NO LONGER STEERS OFF THE CONTRACT SYMBOL. It asked for "the lookup surface it
#      exposes to the rest of the codebase"; the sense arm answered that literally, found
#      the finder concern, and spent five calls walking one method at a time. Step 1 now
#      ends ON the record class - it asks which single record class the ticket is about and
#      what a rework must preserve, and says the audit that follows is about the class as a
#      whole and not any one part of it. Step 2 then starts where the gold lives.
#   2. THE AXIS NAMES A NEW MECHANISM: these dependents pass through NO shared entry point.
#      There is no method, helper or gateway they all go through - each reaches the record
#      class itself, so enumerating what calls any one part of it cannot find them. That is
#      a true property of this gold set (measured below) and it is precisely the route that
#      produced 3 of 19 last cycle.
#   3. GOLD RE-SELECTED FROM WHAT THE BASELINE MISSED. The three `dependents` rows the
#      baseline cited - `d:account-owned-concern`, `d:json-ld-helper`,
#      `d:tag-manager-local-lookup` - are the three closest to the finder surface its call 5
#      grepped (`find_local|find_remote|.representative`). All three MOVE to the NON-SCORING
#      `contract` anchor group: both arms reached them, which is the definition of an anchor.
#      Two further candidates (`Admin::ModerationAction#mark_statuses_as_sensitive!`,
#      `Admin::SystemCheck::MediaPrivacyCheck#create_test_attachment!`) were considered and
#      NOT admitted, because both take the dependency through `Account.representative` -
#      the same token that grep already earned the baseline. That is an authoring
#      preference, not a screen: no draft was killed by a grep here.
#   4. SIX NEW ROWS ADMITTED from the shown blast set, in six areas the old gold did not
#      touch at all: a validator, a scheduler, an admin metrics dimension, the base
#      application controller, a search-index importer and a followers-synchronisation
#      controller. Each was opened and its line read by hand.
#
# THE OPEN QUESTION FROM LAST CYCLE, NOW SETTLED. minibench.md flagged that "whether
# `Account` can carry these nineteen at all is untested, because no blast set was ever
# shown". It is tested now and it carries: `sense_blast Account --file app/models/account.rb`
# returns 200 direct callers over 30 areas, and every one of the 22 `dependents` rows below
# appears in that shown payload. NOT a NO-ANCHOR.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE CONTRACT
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `Account` (app/models/account.rb) is the record every other model, service, worker and
# controller in Mastodon hangs off: local users and remote actors are both rows in it. It is
# the thing a maintainer reworking identity storage would actually open first. Anchor
# UNCHANGED from cycle 1 - the loop does not re-scout a contract that has been measured.
#
# SEAM PROFILE (bench/lib/seam_hunt.py, `Account --file app/models/account.rb`, re-run this
# cycle, unchanged from cycle 2):
#   app caller files : 107   (total incl test/non-app: 107)
#   SCATTER (dirs)   : 34
#   GREP-NOISE       : 'Account' in 257 app files   PRECISION=0.42
#   VERDICT          : SCATTERED + GREP-NOISY
# The three candidates profiled in cycle 2 are kept on the record so a later cycle does not
# repeat them; none beat 0.42:
#   Account                 0.42  (107 callers / 257 grep files, 34 dirs)  <- kept
#   ResolveAccountService   0.94  (16 callers / 17 grep files, 9 dirs) - near-transcription,
#     the profile laws.md records as handing a baseline 17 of 18 rows in one grep. REJECTED.
#   AccountReachFinder      1.17  (7 callers / 6 grep files, 3 dirs) - above 1.00 means false
#     caller edges, and 7 files cannot yield twelve rows anyway. REJECTED.
#   AccountStat             RESOLVER-GAP (0 app caller files).
# Two facet hunts, also kept on the record as dead ends:
#   - `Account::Interactions`: `sense_blast` returns ZERO direct callers; its 20 indirect
#     callers are all "via Account", i.e. the same caller set one hop out.
#   - Instance-method dispatch does not resolve across files here. `sense_graph
#     Account#local? --direction callers` returns 12 callers, ALL inside account.rb; the
#     seventeen `Account::Interactions` predicates return 3 app caller files between them
#     across 2 directories, every other caller a spec. There is no method-level facet.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE AXIS (the whole thesis, and what the mini-bench measures)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The dependents of this contract share NO entry point. There is no method, no helper, no
# gateway that they pass through: each one reaches the record class directly, and it does so
# in whatever form the surrounding code already had - a type test, a scope chain, a class
# constant, an aggregate, a raw SQL call, an ActiveModel name. So enumerating the callers of
# any one PART of the contract cannot reach them; only the class as a whole has them all.
# And because most of these files are not about accounts, the record's name recurs in them
# for reasons that have nothing to do with the dependency, so finding the file is not
# finding the dependency - one line is.
#
# MEASURED SUPPORT FOR THE MECHANISM, on this gold set. Of the 22 `dependents` rows, ZERO
# call any of the five methods the cycle-2 sense arm walked (`find_local`, `find_remote`,
# `representative`, `find_local!`, `find_remote!`) - the three rows that DID sit near that
# surface are exactly the three that moved to the anchor group. The 22 remaining lines
# reach the class through 14 distinct expressions: `.find`, `.exists?`, `.where`,
# `.sum`, `.local`, `.inboxes`, `.model_name`, `.find_by_sql`, `.find_or_initialize_by`,
# `.without_suspended`, `.without_internal`, `.searchable`, `is_a?`/`when`, and two class
# constants (`Account::MENTION_RE`, `Account::URL_PREFIX_RE`). No method-caller walk
# enumerates that, and no single expression covers more than a handful of rows.
#
# WHAT A GREP PRINTS, RECORDED AND NEVER A GATE (laws.md: NO GREP SCREEN IS A GATE, IN ANY
# FORM). `Account` appears in 257 app files against 107 real caller files - precision 0.42,
# the lowest profiled on this repo. Last cycle's baseline ran TEN distinct greps against
# this and reached 3 of 19; the negative-filter shape of two of them (`| grep -vE ...`) is
# the tell that it was drowning in occurrences and pruning by hand. This is RECORDED; it
# decides nothing, and the two-arm run in the next phase is what decides.
#
# WHAT THE ARM IS SHOWN. `sense_blast Account` is AMBIGUOUS at MCP defaults (13 symbols named
# Account; the tool returns a hint naming the `file` parameter plus top matches, so an arm
# pays one extra call to disambiguate). `sense_blast Account --file app/models/account.rb`
# returns 200 direct callers over 30 areas, risk high, truncated. EVERY one of the 22
# `dependents` rows below appears in that shown set, and each row's line sits INSIDE the
# enclosing `def` the payload names - checked row by row, because the blast payload gives
# the enclosing `def`, not the line that touches the contract. Each line below was then
# opened and read by hand this cycle (all 22 re-read at the current checkout).
#
# MEMORIZATION (memorization_probe.py, per candidate row). CUT as recited and staying cut:
# `FeedManager` (0.727), `InstancePresenter` (0.842). The six rows admitted this cycle were
# all probed: `NoteLengthValidator`, `Scheduler::SelfDestructScheduler`,
# `Admin::Metrics::Dimension::SpaceUsageDimension`, `Importer::StatusesIndexImporter` and
# `ActivityPub::FollowersSynchronizationsController` all declare too few members to score
# recitation (bar inapplicable, 0-1 members); `ApplicationController` came back at recall
# 0.30 naming only 3 members, which the probe itself labels "generic framework vocabulary,
# not recitation of THIS symbol" - and its credit here is a line-level fact
# (`Account.without_internal.exists?` at :108), not a member list. The anchor itself comes
# back recited (`Account` 0.312) - that is the contract's own API surface, which is why the
# contract centre is a NON-SCORING anchor group; no gold row's credit is a member list.
description: |
  You are a maintainer about to rework how a user account record is stored and looked
  up - the record that both local users and remote actors are rows in. Before you touch
  it, audit what depends on that record, completely enough that the rework cannot
  silently break a dependent. What counts is the exact line at which a dependency is
  taken, not the file it sits in: for each one give an exact file:line a teammate could
  jump straight to, plus one phrase on how it uses the record. A filename with no line
  number does not count, and a missed dependent is a regression shipped.
steps:
- name: Identify the record under change
  prompt: "Task: orient. In a few sentences plus exact file:line references, name the
    single record this ticket is about, say where it is defined, and say what a rework of
    it would have to preserve. Settle on the record as a whole - the audit that follows is
    about everything that depends on it, not about any one part of it. Give file:line for
    everything you name.
    "
  checks:
  - type: response_richness
    value: '3'
    required: true
  - type: mcp_tool_used
    value: sense_graph
    required: false
    layer: adoption
- name: Audit every dependent of the account record
  prompt: "Task: this is the core of the ticket. Find EVERY place in the codebase that
    depends on the record you just identified, so the rework cannot silently break one. Be
    exhaustive and group them by area. These dependents share no entry point: there is no
    method, helper or gateway they all pass through, so enumerating what calls any one part
    of the record will not find them - each one reaches the record itself, in whatever form
    the surrounding code already used, and there is no single shape to look for. Most of
    them are not about accounts at all: they consult the record to settle a question about
    something else entirely. In those files the record's name also recurs many times over
    for reasons that have nothing to do with the dependency, so identifying the file is not
    the same as identifying the dependency: one line in it is the dependency, and that line
    is what I need. For each dependent give file:line and one phrase on how it uses the
    record. A filename with no line number does not count, and a missed dependent is a
    regression shipped.
    "
  checks:
  - type: response_richness
    value: '6'
    required: true
    description: Pinned the dependency line in each file, not just the file
  - type: no_grep
    value: no_grep
    required: false
    layer: adoption
  - type: mcp_tool_used
    value: sense_blast
    required: false
    layer: adoption
scoring:
  weights:
    correctness: 0.70
    efficiency: 0.30
# Gold is the must-find audit of what depends on the account record. TWO groups:
#   - `contract` (7, NON-SCORING anchor): the record itself, the obvious centre both arms
#     reach, and the three rows the cycle-2 baseline actually cited. It does not
#     discriminate and it is not meant to.
#   - `dependents` (22, THE discriminator): ONE row per FILE, across 18 directories. Every
#     row is in the shown `sense_blast` output above, every row's line sits inside the
#     enclosing `def` that payload names, and every credit below was read off its own line
#     by hand (gold_audit stamp/verify), never taken from a script tally.
gold:
  # --- NON-SCORING anchors: the contract centre, plus the three rows cycle 2 measured BOTH arms reaching ---
  - {id: contract-model, group: contract, match: [models/account.rb], relation: "app/models/account.rb:65 `class Account < ApplicationRecord` - the account record itself, the contract under change"}
  - {id: c:status, group: contract, match: [models/status.rb], relation: "app/models/status.rb:77 `belongs_to :account, inverse_of: :statuses` - the content model hangs off the account association"}
  - {id: c:user, group: contract, match: [models/user.rb], relation: "app/models/user.rb:72 `belongs_to :account, inverse_of: :user` - a local login is a User row pointing at an Account row"}
  - {id: c:resolve-service, group: contract, match: [services/resolve_account_service.rb], relation: "app/services/resolve_account_service.rb:27 `@account ||= Account.find_remote(@username, @domain)` - the webfinger resolve path, the obvious lookup entry point for accounts"}
  - {id: c:account-owned-concern, group: contract, match: [account_owned_concern.rb], relation: "app/controllers/concerns/account_owned_concern.rb:21 `@account = username_param.present? ? Account.find_local!(username_param) : Account.local.find(account_id_param)` - the shared account-owned page concern resolves its subject through two class finders; BOTH arms cited it in cycle 2"}
  - {id: c:json-ld-helper, group: contract, match: [helpers/json_ld_helper.rb], relation: "app/helpers/json_ld_helper.rb:233 `on_behalf_of ||= Account.representative` - unsigned fetches fall back to the instance representative account; BOTH arms cited it in cycle 2"}
  - {id: c:tag-manager-local-lookup, group: contract, match: [activitypub/tag_manager.rb], relation: "app/lib/activitypub/tag_manager.rb:260 `Account.local.with_username(usernames).or(Account.local.where(id: ids))` - URI-to-actor translation resolves local actor URIs through the class scope; BOTH arms cited it in cycle 2"}
  # --- THE DISCRIMINATOR: one dependency line per file, in a file whose subject is elsewhere ---
  - {id: d:activity-uri-resource, group: dependents, match: [activitypub/activity.rb], relation: "app/lib/activitypub/activity.rb:75 `ActivityPub::TagManager.instance.uri_to_resource(uri, Account)` - inbound activity handling hands the record class to a generic URI resolver as the type to resolve into"}
  - {id: d:activity-create-delivered-to, group: dependents, match: [activity/create.rb], relation: "app/lib/activitypub/activity/create.rb:170 `@delivered_to_account ||= Account.find(@options[:delivered_to_account_id])` - status creation memoises the delivery target by id to decide local visibility"}
  - {id: d:favourited-by-accounts, group: dependents, match: [statuses/favourited_by_accounts_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/api/v1/statuses/favourited_by_accounts_controller.rb:22 `Account` heading a multi-line chain into `.without_suspended.includes(:favourites, :account_stat, :user)` - the favourited-by list builds its preload scope off the bare class"}
  - {id: d:reblogged-by-accounts, group: dependents, match: [statuses/reblogged_by_accounts_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/api/v1/statuses/reblogged_by_accounts_controller.rb:22 `Account.without_suspended.includes(:statuses, :account_stat, :user).references(:statuses)` - the reblogged-by list builds its preload scope off the class"}
  - {id: d:authorize-interactions-dispatch, group: dependents, match: [authorize_interactions_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/authorize_interactions_controller.rb:11 `when Account` - the remote-follow landing page branches on the resolved resource being an account rather than a status"}
  - {id: d:signature-verification, group: dependents, match: [concerns/signature_verification.rb], relation: "app/controllers/concerns/signature_verification.rb:48 `signed_request_actor.is_a?(Account) ? signed_request_actor : nil` - HTTP signature verification type-tests the signing actor against the class before treating it as an account"}
  - {id: d:inbox-unknown-actor, group: dependents, match: [activitypub/inboxes_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/activitypub/inboxes_controller.rb:30 `... && !Account.exists?(uri: json['actor'])` - the last clause of a five-clause boolean drops Delete/Update activities for actors the instance has never stored"}
  - {id: d:followers-sync-uri-prefix, group: dependents, match: [activitypub/followers_synchronizations_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/activitypub/followers_synchronizations_controller.rb:20 `signed_request_account.uri[Account::URL_PREFIX_RE]` - follower-list synchronisation slices a partner's URI with a pattern constant declared on the record class"}
  - {id: d:admin-api-set-account, group: dependents, match: [v1/admin/accounts_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/api/v1/admin/accounts_controller.rb:103 `@account = Account.find(params[:id])` - the admin API resolves its subject by primary key; the file's other thirteen mentions of the name are serializers, services, workers and filters"}
  - {id: d:admin-base-set-user, group: dependents, match: [admin/base_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/admin/base_controller.rb:21 `@user = Account.find(params[:account_id]).user || raise(ActiveRecord::RecordNotFound)` - the admin base controller reaches a login by going through the account row first"}
  - {id: d:single-user-mode, group: dependents, match: [controllers/application_controller.rb], relation: "app/controllers/application_controller.rb:108 `@single_user_mode ||= Rails.configuration.x.single_user_mode && Account.without_internal.exists?` - the base controller decides whether the whole instance runs in single-user mode by counting non-internal account rows"}
  - {id: d:serializer-decorator-model-name, group: dependents, match: [rest/account_serializer.rb], relation: "app/serializers/rest/account_serializer.rb:29 `Account.model_name` - a SimpleDelegator wrapper asks the class for its ActiveModel name so a moved-account delegate serialises as an account"}
  - {id: d:fetch-remote-actor-typecheck, group: dependents, match: [fetch_remote_account_service.rb], relation: "app/services/activitypub/fetch_remote_account_service.rb:7 `return actor if actor.nil? || actor.is_a?(Account)` - remote actor fetching type-tests the fetched actor against the class and rejects anything else"}
  - {id: d:admin-deletion-worker, group: dependents, match: [admin/account_deletion_worker.rb], relation: "app/workers/admin/account_deletion_worker.rb:9 `delete_account = Account.find(account_id)` - the deletion job rehydrates the record from an id carried across the queue boundary"}
  - {id: d:self-destruct-inboxes, group: dependents, match: [scheduler/self_destruct_scheduler.rb], relation: "app/workers/scheduler/self_destruct_scheduler.rb:54 `@inboxes ||= Account.inboxes` - the instance self-destruct scheduler memoises every known delivery inbox off the class before tearing the instance down"}
  - {id: d:account-batch-form, group: dependents, match: [form/account_batch.rb], relation: "app/models/form/account_batch.rb:69 `Account.where(id: account_ids)` - the admin bulk-action form resolves its checked ids back to records through the class"}
  - {id: d:suggestions-source, group: dependents, match: [account_suggestions/source.rb], relation: "app/models/account_suggestions/source.rb:13 `Account` heading a multi-line chain into `.searchable.where(discoverable: true).without_silenced.without_memorial` - the follow-suggestion base scope is chained off the bare class"}
  - {id: d:friends-of-friends, group: dependents, match: [friends_of_friends_source.rb], relation: "app/models/account_suggestions/friends_of_friends_source.rb:10 `Account.find_by_sql([<<~SQL.squish, { id: account.id, limit: limit }])` - the friends-of-friends suggestion runs raw SQL through the account class"}
  - {id: d:action-log-filter, group: dependents, match: [admin/action_log_filter.rb], relation: "app/models/admin/action_log_filter.rb:114 `account = Account.find_or_initialize_by(id: value)` - filtering the audit log by target builds an unsaved account to match the polymorphic target on"}
  - {id: d:note-length-mention-re, group: dependents, match: [validators/note_length_validator.rb], relation: "app/validators/note_length_validator.rb:19 `new_text.gsub!(Account::MENTION_RE, '@\\2')` - the profile-note length validator strips mentions using a pattern constant declared on the record class before counting graphemes"}
  - {id: d:space-usage-avatar-sum, group: dependents, match: [dimension/space_usage_dimension.rb], relation: "app/lib/admin/metrics/dimension/space_usage_dimension.rb:44 `Account.sum(Arel.sql('COALESCE(avatar_file_size, 0) + COALESCE(header_file_size, 0)'))` - the admin storage dashboard adds avatar and header bytes by aggregating raw columns over the class"}
  - {id: d:statuses-index-local-votes, group: dependents, match: [importer/statuses_index_importer.rb], relation: "app/lib/importer/statuses_index_importer.rb:74 `Poll.joins(:votes).where(votes: { account: Account.local })` - the search-index importer restricts which poll votes get indexed by joining against the class's local scope"}
